    <div style="background:#0d2f33;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #4dd0e1;margin-bottom:20px;">
    <h3 style="color:#e0f7fa;margin-top:0;">🧠 Lesson Summary</h3>
    <p>Data is raw facts; information is processed, meaningful data. ICT is the use of computing and communication technologies to process and share information. The information processing cycle has input, processing, output and storage, with feedback. Good information is accurate, relevant, timely, complete and clear; bad data gives bad results (GIGO).</p>
    <h4 style="color:#e0f7fa;margin:16px 0 6px 0;">🗒️ Revision notes</h4>
    <ul style="margin:6px 0;padding-left:22px;">
    <li>Key terms.</li>
    <li>Data vs information.</li>
    <li>Processing cycle.</li>
    <li>Qualities of information.</li>
    </ul>
    </div>
